ce-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257rig-c17"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-c17"],"id":"long.record-257rig-c17","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.85 (Terminal bounds at unbounded depths)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.85, p. 68, label record:257rig-c17","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that for every $N\\ge0$ there are $M\\ge\\max\\{N,1\\}$ and $D\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,M\\}$ such that\n$$\n|\\operatorname{ihc}(D,M-1)|\\le B(M)\n       =2\\lfloor\\sqrt M\\rfloor+4.\n$$\nThen some infinite $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}_{>0}$ satisfies $X_A(2)=1/2$. No compatibility between different finite supports or bound on their earlier carries is required.*\n\n*These are not the exact-row conditions of Definition 6.66. For such a finite support,\n$$\n\\operatorname{ihc}(D,M-1)=2^{M-1}-Q(D,M),\n$$\nso an exact row has carry $1$, whereas the displayed bound allows several positive and negative values. At $M=6$, for example, $D=\\{2,3\\}$ has $Q(D,6)=30$ and carry $2$: it satisfies the terminal bound but is not an exact row. Both cofinal existence statements nevertheless imply, and are implied by, half-membership, as explained in Proposition 2.7. The difference between their finite data must not be confused with a strict logical weakening of the membership problem.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257rig-c17","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257rig-c17","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_both_cofinal_statements_iff_half_membership%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_both_cofinal_statements_iff_half_membership%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_both_cofinal_statements_iff_half_membership"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257rig-c17","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_row_integerHalfCarry_eq_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_row_integerHalfCarry_eq_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_row_integerHalfCarry_eq_one"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257rig-c17","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_integerHalfCarry_eq_two_pow_sub_localPrefixQuotient%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c17%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_integerHalfCarry_eq_two_pow_sub_localPrefixQuotient%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858